  "id": "binaural-cue",
  "term": "binaural cue",
  "definition": "A binaural cue is information the brain gets by comparing what arrives at the two ears to help locate a sound. In this packet, the binaural cue discussed is interaural time difference, meaning small differences in when a sound reaches each ear.",
